From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:00:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gluon-mesh-batman-adv: announce the NAT64 prefix in
 router advertisements

radvd/arguments has been dying on every start of gluon-radvd since
97a0d9a4 ("radvd/arguments: Announce parker node's prefix and DNS")
dropped the gluon.site import but kept the site.radvd() lookups at the
end of the script. uradvd still received the prefix and the RDNSS
address, because Lua had already flushed those to stdout by the time the
script hit the undefined global, but site.radvd.preferred_lifetime and
site.radvd.valid_lifetime were silently never applied. Restore the
import.

While here, announce the NAT64 prefix (RFC 8781) when /tmp/pref64
exists. noderoute writes that file on the nodes that translate IPv4 for
their clients, and only there: --pref64 needs uradvd from the
freifunkMUC fork (implemented in c472302, pinned by site-ffm at
780182a), and a uradvd built without it rejects the unknown option and
exits before sending a single advertisement.

Reading the runtime files through gluon.util.readfile also gets rid of
the duplicated local and of the space indentation the script picked up
in 97a0d9a4, which luacheck and editorconfig-checker had both been
complaining about.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments          | 28 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments
index d44f8a3e..1fae015e 100755
--- a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments
+++ b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/luasrc/lib/gluon/radvd/arguments
@@ -1,20 +1,28 @@
 #!/usr/bin/lua
 
-local f = io.open("/tmp/range6","r")
-if f then
-    local range6 = f:read('*a')
-    f:close()
+local site = require "gluon.site"
+local util = require "gluon.util"
 
-    io.write("-i br-client -p " .. range6)
+-- noderoute writes these files while it configures the client network, so
+-- uradvd only picks up changes when it is restarted afterwards.
+
+local range6 = util.readfile("/tmp/range6")
+if range6 then
+	io.write("-i br-client -p " .. range6)
 end
 
-local f = io.open("/tmp/addr6","r")
-if f then
-    local addr6 = f:read('*a')
-    f:close()
+local addr6 = util.readfile("/tmp/addr6")
+if addr6 then
+	io.write(" --rdnss " .. addr6)
+end
 
-    io.write(" --rdnss " .. addr6)
+-- Only a node that translates IPv4 for its clients announces a NAT64
+-- prefix (RFC 8781); the file is absent on all other nodes.
+local pref64 = util.readfile("/tmp/pref64")
+if pref64 then
+	io.write(" --pref64 " .. pref64)
 end
+
 if site.radvd() then
 	if site.radvd.preferred_lifetime() then
 		io.write(" --preferred-lifetime " .. site.radvd.preferred_lifetime())
-- 
